#
# Re-apply the active Perf Control profile's CPU/GPU clock caps after resume.
# Deep suspend offlines every non-boot CPU; a cpufreq policy whose CPUs ALL go
# offline (the big cluster - e.g. policy6 = cpu6/7 on SM8750) is torn down and
# recreated at resume with factory limits, silently dropping the profile's
# scaling_max_freq cap while the profile still reads as active. The boot CPU's
# policy and the GPU devfreq are untouched, so only the big cluster reverts
# (proven on AYN Odin 3: policy6 3072000 -> 4089600 across a cpu6/7 hotplug
# cycle). Clocks only, foreground: the fan curve is owned by the fancontrol
# service / Decky plugin which persist on their own, and we want the caps back
# before the session resumes rendering.

[ -x /usr/bin/perfcontrol ] && /usr/bin/perfcontrol boot >/dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
